<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vijaya Ranga Chokkanatha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1731</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vijaya Ranga Chokkanatha was ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madurai">Madurai</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayak</a> kingdom from 1706 until his death in the early 1730s, succeeding the regency of his grandmother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rani-mangammal">Rani Mangammal</a>. His long reign was largely peaceful, but he left government to his ministers and was known mainly for his piety and gifts to temples. He died without a son, and the succession dispute under his widow Meenakshi brought the kingdom to its end.</p></div>
